{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3196","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3196","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3196\",\"parent_revision\":\"22e4f00590877fec1afea690b85ad5ab789db65258bb2ec7d326b7bdc2bb77a3\",\"root_revision\":\"22e4f00590877fec1afea690b85ad5ab789db65258bb2ec7d326b7bdc2bb77a3\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-23\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nGoal: `backlog_groom(selector=..., section=..., content=...)` should wrap arbitrary section content into exactly one entry block per write.\\n\\nReproduction: `dh:alignment-analyst` wrote to #3187's \\\"Design Intent Alignment\\\" section via `backlog_groom` with content whose first line was itself a `## Design Intent Alignment` markdown header followed by `Alignment assessment: **ALIGNED**` body text. Reading the section back afterward via `backlog_view(selector=\\\"#3187\\\", summary=False, sections=[\\\"Design Intent Alignment\\\"])` shows two entries instead of one:\\n\\n```\\nentries: [\\n  {\\\"id\\\": \\\"0000-00-00T00:00:00Z\\\", \\\"struck\\\": false, \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div><sub>2026-08-23T11:56:18.965325Z</sub>\\\"},\\n  {\\\"id\\\": \\\"0000-00-00T00:00:00Z\\\", \\\"struck\\\": false, \\\"content\\\": \\\"Alignment assessment: **ALIGNED**\\\"}\\n]\\n```\\n\\nThe first \\\"entry\\\" is a literal, unparsed `<div><sub>{timestamp}</sub>` wrapper fragment \u2014 the parser's own entry-open marker \u2014 surfaced as if it were content, carrying the zero-date sentinel id. The real content (the `## Design Intent Alignment` header line plus body) is split across two entries with the heading line apparently swallowed/lost.\\n\\nImpact: This is the same defect class this session has been chasing all day in `entry_blocks.py`'s wrap/parse boundary (see #3187, #3190, and the entry-id merge sprint handoff's \\\"central finding\\\") \u2014 a caller consuming this section via the progressive-disclosure path would see the raw wrapper markup as live content and would not reliably find \\\"Alignment assessment:\\\" text load-bearing logic depends on, because it landed in a second, oddly-scoped entry rather than staying attached to its heading.\\n\\nNot established: whether the trigger is specifically \\\"content whose own first line is a markdown heading matching the section name\\\" (a self-referential heading collision) or something broader about how `backlog_groom` wraps already-multi-line content. Needs a minimal reproduction isolated from the agent-authored content that surfaced it.\\n\\nUser-provided context: the underlying agent's Write content began with `## Design Intent Alignment\\\\ n\\\\nAlignment assessment: **ALIGNED**\\\\n\\\\n...` \u2014 i.e. it restated the section's own heading as the first line of its content, which may be the actual trigger rather than a `backlog_groom`/entry_blocks defect.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation while grooming #3187, 2026-08-23\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-23\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"9491abe20e8fa8d3fac026aa0ef97d1cf694fedf581b060ef1166a77ccdd351f\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABQTRwkQ\"}"}